# Executor-tier configuration for the slice-executor subagents.
# Copy to .env, uncomment/edit the keys you want to change, then apply:
#
#   python3 scripts/workflow.py sync-agents
#
# Unset keys keep the built-in defaults (the values shown below). Values are
# written verbatim into the agent files, so model aliases (opus/sonnet/haiku),
# full model IDs, or `inherit` all work without code changes.
# Set an *_EFFORT key to empty to omit the effort line entirely — required for
# models that reject the effort parameter (e.g. haiku). Models may not be empty.
# .env is gitignored; this example file is machinery and tracks upstream.
# After /update-workspace, re-run sync-agents (updates reset the agent files
# to upstream defaults; `validate` warns while they drift).

# Claude Code (.claude/agents/slice-executor-{low,mid,high}.md)
#SLICE_EXECUTOR_LOW_MODEL=haiku
#SLICE_EXECUTOR_LOW_EFFORT=
#SLICE_EXECUTOR_MID_MODEL=sonnet
#SLICE_EXECUTOR_MID_EFFORT=xhigh
#SLICE_EXECUTOR_HIGH_MODEL=opus
#SLICE_EXECUTOR_HIGH_EFFORT=xhigh

# Codex (.codex/agents/slice-executor-{low,mid,high}.toml)
#CODEX_SLICE_EXECUTOR_LOW_MODEL=gpt-5.5
#CODEX_SLICE_EXECUTOR_LOW_EFFORT=medium
#CODEX_SLICE_EXECUTOR_MID_MODEL=gpt-5.5
#CODEX_SLICE_EXECUTOR_MID_EFFORT=high
#CODEX_SLICE_EXECUTOR_HIGH_MODEL=gpt-5.5
#CODEX_SLICE_EXECUTOR_HIGH_EFFORT=xhigh
